# The memory bank is a record: append a file, never edit a shared one. That rule is
# what keeps it out of every pull request's conflict list, and this line is the
# safety net for the one file the rule cannot cover.
#
# `merge=union` takes BOTH sides of a conflicting hunk instead of stopping. It is right
# here and wrong almost everywhere else: it is only safe for a file whose lines are
# unordered, independent, and meaningless in combination with their neighbours. An index
# of one-line-per-record is exactly that. A config file, a lockfile or anything with
# syntax is not - union would happily produce a file that parses as neither side.
#
# The cost is that a genuine edit to the SAME line on both sides silently keeps both
# copies rather than asking. For an index that means one duplicated row, fixed by
# deleting a line - and found by reading the file, not by running `rk memory find`,
# which searches the live bank under the state root and never opens this copy. That
# is the trade, taken knowingly.
#
# `memory-bank/decisions/*` is deliberately NOT listed here, and the omission is the
# considered half of this file. A decision record is prose with structure - headings,
# a stated decision, its consequences - so it fails union's precondition outright.
# Where the one-file-per-record rule holds, two records never touch the same path, the
# attribute never fires, and it is inert. Where the rule breaks - two records taking
# the same date and the same slug, or a later edit to one - it fires, and it resolves
# the collision CLEAN at exit 0 by concatenating both documents: a record asserting
# "capped at 3" and one asserting "unbounded" become a single file asserting both,
# under one `## Decision` heading, with nothing to say it happened. Without the
# attribute git stops with `CONFLICT (add/add)` and a human picks. So the line is
# worthless in every case it was argued for and destructive in the only case it acts,
# and a record that cannot be trusted to say what was decided is worth less than a
# conflict somebody has to resolve.
memory-bank/index.md      merge=union
